{"name":"Mexicali Rose","hex":"#e39b99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mexicali Rose (1929 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mexicali Rose is a 1929 American pre-Code romantic drama film directed by Erle C. Kenton, and starring Barbara Stanwyck and Sam Hardy. A silent and sound version are preserved at the Library of Congress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Mexicali_Rose_1929_Poster.jpg/330px-Mexicali_Rose_1929_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexicali_Rose_(1929_film)","wikidata":"Q3307662"},{"title":"Mexicali Rose (1939 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mexicali Rose is a 1939 American Western film directed by George Sherman and starring Gene Autry, Smiley Burnette, and Noah Beery. Based on a story by Luci Ward and Connie Lee, the film is about a singing cowboy who fights corrupt oil men selling worthless stock from a non-existent well located on land belonging to a poor Mexican orphanage."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/Mexicali_Rose_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexicali_Rose_(1939_film)","wikidata":"Q6825735"},{"title":"Mexicali Rose (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Mexicali Rose\" is a popular song composed by bandleader and pianist Jack Breckenridge Tenney in the early 1920s, when he and his seven piece orchestra played the hotels and clubs of the Calexico and Mexicali border. The song became a hit in the mid-1930s, thanks to Gene Autry and Bing Crosby, around the same time that Tenney became a lawyer and was elected to the California State Assembly. Tenney was later appointed to head of the California Senate Factfinding Subcommittee on Un-American Activities."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/Gene-autry-mexicali-rose-perfect.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexicali_Rose_(song)","wikidata":"Q6825733"},{"title":"Mexicali","blocks":[{"text":"Mexicali is the capital city of the Mexican state of Baja California. The city, which abuts the Mexico–United States border and the U.S. city of Calexico, California, is the seat of the Mexicali Municipality. It has a population of 689,775, according to the 2010 census, while the Calexico–Mexicali metropolitan area is home to a combined population of 1,000,000. Mexicali is a regional economic and cultural hub for the border region of The Californias."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Rectoria-uabc_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Rectoria-uabc_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexicali","wikidata":"Q199440"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Mexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg/250px-Mexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Mexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Mexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg/250px-Mexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMexicali_Rose_sheet_music.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Plaza_Calafia_-_panoramio_-_rocksas_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Plaza_Cal